ny less  legitimate you are just trying to have a  superiority complex over another player  because you beat a boss in a harder way  and it's kind of sad  gate keeping a mainly single player game  like are you okay do you really not have  anything better to do there's plenty of  amazing players out there who do these  difficult challenge runs but also don't  shove it in other people's faces it's  like that kid in school who will ask all  the other kids in the class what they  got on a test because they know they got  the hundred percent and probably did  better than them i believe those kids  were always known as  annoying the souls game community has a  pretty bad reputation for doing exactly  this so i wish people would just stop  doing it but i don't think that's  possible unfortunately so why am i  talking about all this in a let me solo  her video because this is the exact  opposite experience of what all of the  gatekeeping players want while also  having a single guy out there doing that  exact experience that they try to gate  keep on to people and i find that  hilarious this guy is basically telling  people to not play the game saying i got  this don't even try just sit back relax  and watch a master go to work and i love  it based on what i've seen most people  are loving it too in a community where  the only help people usually get is  someone saying get good there's this guy  who goes against the hardest boss in the  game and beats this boss for people like  it's his job he even has a schedule  where he's usually there between 3 to 8  pm cst i found a message on reddit that  says he feels bad when he messes up and  fails he says sometimes the lag between  the host and myself is too much and i  get killed instantly or miss the crucial  dodge timing on melania's waterfowl  dance i would like to express my apology  to those i have failed like what a nice  guy man he's just trying to help others  and in a gaming community that's really  rare to see whitney h